{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41602",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/apache/thrift: Apache Thrift: Integer Overflow in TFramedTransport Go implementation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Integer Overflow or Wraparound vulnerability in Apache Thrift TFramedTransport Go language implementation\n\nThis issue affects Apache Thrift: before 0.23.0.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 0.23.0, which fixes the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41602",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41602\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/apache/thrift\nFixed Version: 0.23.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-41602](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41602)\nInteger Overflow or Wraparound vulnerability in Apache Thrift TFramedTransport Go language implementation\n\nThis issue affects Apache Thrift: before 0.23.0.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 0.23.0, which fixes the issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41602**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/apache/thrift|0.23.0|[CVE-2026-41602](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41602)|\n\nInteger Overflow or Wraparound vulnerability in Apache Thrift TFramedTransport Go language implementation\n\nThis issue affects Apache Thrift: before 0.23.0.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 0.23.0, which fixes the issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of Service due to Panic in AWS SDK for Go v2 SDK EventStream Decoder"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "**CVSSv3.1 Rating**: [Medium]\n**CVSSv3.1 Score**: [5.9]\n**CVSSv3.1 Vector String**: [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]\n\n## Summary and Impact\nAn issue exists in the the EventStream header decoder in AWS SDK for Go v2 in versions predating [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23). An actor can send a malformed EventStream response frame containing a crafted header value type byte outside the valid range, which can cause the host process to terminate.\n\nImpacted versions: \u003c [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23)\n\n## Patches\nThis issue has been addressed in versions [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23) and above. We recommend upgrading to the latest version and ensuring any forked or derivative code is patched to incorporate the new fixes. \n\n## Workarounds\nNot Applicable\n\n## References\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, we ask that you contact [AWS/Amazon] Security via our [vulnerability reporting page](https://aws.amazon.com/security/vulnerability-reporting) or directly via email to [aws-security@amazon.com](mailto:aws-security@amazon.com). Please do not create a public GitHub issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/s3\nFixed Version: 1.97.3\nLink: [GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2)\n**CVSSv3.1 Rating**: [Medium]\n**CVSSv3.1 Score**: [5.9]\n**CVSSv3.1 Vector String**: [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]\n\n## Summary and Impact\nAn issue exists in the the EventStream header decoder in AWS SDK for Go v2 in versions predating [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23). An actor can send a malformed EventStream response frame containing a crafted header value type byte outside the valid range, which can cause the host process to terminate.\n\nImpacted versions: \u003c [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23)\n\n## Patches\nThis issue has been addressed in versions [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23) and above. We recommend upgrading to the latest version and ensuring any forked or derivative code is patched to incorporate the new fixes. \n\n## Workarounds\nNot Applicable\n\n## References\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, we ask that you contact [AWS/Amazon] Security via our [vulnerability reporting page](https://aws.amazon.com/security/vulnerability-reporting) or directly via email to [aws-security@amazon.com](mailto:aws-security@amazon.com). Please do not create a public GitHub issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/s3|1.97.3|[GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xmrv-pmrh-hhx2)|\n\n**CVSSv3.1 Rating**: [Medium]\n**CVSSv3.1 Score**: [5.9]\n**CVSSv3.1 Vector String**: [CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]\n\n## Summary and Impact\nAn issue exists in the the EventStream header decoder in AWS SDK for Go v2 in versions predating [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23). An actor can send a malformed EventStream response frame containing a crafted header value type byte outside the valid range, which can cause the host process to terminate.\n\nImpacted versions: \u003c [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23)\n\n## Patches\nThis issue has been addressed in versions [2026-03-23](https://github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/releases/tag/release-2026-03-23) and above. We recommend upgrading to the latest version and ensuring any forked or derivative code is patched to incorporate the new fixes. \n\n## Workarounds\nNot Applicable\n\n## References\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, we ask that you contact [AWS/Amazon] Security via our [vulnerability reporting page](https://aws.amazon.com/security/vulnerability-reporting) or directly via email to [aws-security@amazon.com](mailto:aws-security@amazon.com). Please do not create a public GitHub issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.9,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41889",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/jackc/pgx: golang: pgx: SQL injection via specific SQL query conditions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "pgx is a PostgreSQL driver and toolkit for Go. Prior to version 5.9.2, SQL injection can occur when the non-default simple protocol is used, a dollar quoted string literal is used in the SQL query, that string literal contains text that would be would be interpreted as a placeholder outside of a string literal, and the value of that placeholder is controllable by the attacker. This issue has been patched in version 5.9.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41889",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41889\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/jackc/pgx/v5\nFixed Version: 5.9.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-41889](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41889)\npgx is a PostgreSQL driver and toolkit for Go. Prior to version 5.9.2, SQL injection can occur when the non-default simple protocol is used, a dollar quoted string literal is used in the SQL query, that string literal contains text that would be would be interpreted as a placeholder outside of a string literal, and the value of that placeholder is controllable by the attacker. This issue has been patched in version 5.9.2.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41889**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/jackc/pgx/v5|5.9.2|[CVE-2026-41889](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41889)|\n\npgx is a PostgreSQL driver and toolkit for Go. Prior to version 5.9.2, SQL injection can occur when the non-default simple protocol is used, a dollar quoted string literal is used in the SQL query, that string literal contains text that would be would be interpreted as a placeholder outside of a string literal, and the value of that placeholder is controllable by the attacker. This issue has been patched in version 5.9.2."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "slack-go `SecretsVerifier` accepts empty signing secret without precondition"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`SecretsVerifier` in slack-go/slack before v0.23.1 accepts an empty signing secret without error. If an application is misconfigured (e.g., an unset or empty `SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET`), `NewSecretsVerifier` builds an HMAC-SHA256 keyed with an empty string, allowing an unauthenticated attacker to forge a valid `X-Slack-Signature` and bypass Slack request authentication. Fixed in v0.23.1, which rejects empty secrets with `ErrInvalidConfiguration`. This is patched in version 0.23.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/slack-go/slack\nFixed Version: 0.23.1\nLink: [GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g)\n`SecretsVerifier` in slack-go/slack before v0.23.1 accepts an empty signing secret without error. If an application is misconfigured (e.g., an unset or empty `SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET`), `NewSecretsVerifier` builds an HMAC-SHA256 keyed with an empty string, allowing an unauthenticated attacker to forge a valid `X-Slack-Signature` and bypass Slack request authentication. Fixed in v0.23.1, which rejects empty secrets with `ErrInvalidConfiguration`. This is patched in version 0.23.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/slack-go/slack|0.23.1|[GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gxhx-2686-5h9g)|\n\n`SecretsVerifier` in slack-go/slack before v0.23.1 accepts an empty signing secret without error. If an application is misconfigured (e.g., an unset or empty `SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET`), `NewSecretsVerifier` builds an HMAC-SHA256 keyed with an empty string, allowing an unauthenticated attacker to forge a valid `X-Slack-Signature` and bypass Slack request authentication. Fixed in v0.23.1, which rejects empty secrets with `ErrInvalidConfiguration`. This is patched in version 0.23.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 4.8,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-2303",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-2303 affecting package telegraf for versions less than 1.29.4-21"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The mongo-go-driver repository contains CGo bindings for GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication on Linux and macOS. The C wrapper implementation contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability due to incorrect assumptions about string termination in the GSSAPI standard. Since GSSAPI buffers are not guaranteed to be null-terminated or have extra padding, this results in reading one byte past the allocated heap buffer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2303",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-2303\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver\nFixed Version: 1.17.7\nLink: [CVE-2026-2303](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2303)\nThe mongo-go-driver repository contains CGo bindings for GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication on Linux and macOS. The C wrapper implementation contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability due to incorrect assumptions about string termination in the GSSAPI standard. Since GSSAPI buffers are not guaranteed to be null-terminated or have extra padding, this results in reading one byte past the allocated heap buffer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-2303**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver|1.17.7|[CVE-2026-2303](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2303)|\n\nThe mongo-go-driver repository contains CGo bindings for GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication on Linux and macOS. The C wrapper implementation contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability due to incorrect assumptions about string termination in the GSSAPI standard. Since GSSAPI buffers are not guaranteed to be null-terminated or have extra padding, this results in reading one byte past the allocated heap buffer."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 6.9,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5932",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unmaintained, unsafe by design, and has known security issues"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GO-2026-5932\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: \nLink: [GO-2026-5932]()\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GO-2026-5932**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/crypto||[GO-2026-5932]()|\n\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
